  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Maritime follow-up Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This mission aims to prepare and implement a mission to Zambia, to work jointly with the Head of the Ministry of Transport, Works, Supply and Communications to formulate terms of reference for seven priority projects in the Zambian Maritime sector given facilitating implementation opportunities by the Dutch Maritime Sector firms and organizations.This mission builds on the Maritime mission (November 2014), based on the needs assessment and prioritization of the Zambian. Upon intensive exchange with the Netherlands Maritime sector, a networking function led to a considerable interest.Before confirmation of the priority projects of the departments, IFIs will be communicated with and visited, given their interest and willingness to support the implementation of the project. The International Financial Institutions (IFIs) will be informed about the mission objectives and create interest in the Dutch Maritime sector involvement in Zambia. Against this background, the mission will consult the IFIs on essential issues and visions and provide for debriefing after the mission.After the mission, there will be a debriefing and presentation of the principal content of the terms of reference. Representatives of different governmental departments will be invited, including IFIs and the Netherlands embassy in Harare, Zimbabwe. The Dutch and local Maritime private sector will be informed.</narrative>
  </description>
